SDUSD::depositCapUsage
├── given the vault has not been seeded
│   ├── it should exempt only an exact initial seed deposit or mint to address(1)
│   ├── it should count an ordinary first deposit and a late seed against the cap
│   ├── it should allow a small pre-seed position to exit without underflow
│   └── it should count a wrong-sized initial deposit to address(1)
├── given the exact initial seed has been deposited
│   ├── it should exclude only the fixed original DUSD seed amount
│   ├── later lock deposits and transfers should not expand the exemption
│   └── rewards earned by the seed should still consume capacity after other holders exit
├── when rewards are notified and released
│   ├── locked rewards should not consume capacity
│   ├── released rewards should consume capacity and may exceed the cap
│   └── exceeding the cap should not block further reward periods or exits
├── when assets exceed the cap
│   └── withdrawals should reopen headroom only after assets fall below the cap
└── when a depositor immediately exits at a higher share price
    ├── repeated round trips should consume capacity only for assets left behind through rounding
    ├── custody through a shared wrapper should not change this behavior
    └── deposits, mints, share transfers, and existing positions should preserve this behavior
